            <ArticleTitle>Neurophysiological measurement of pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurophysiological measurement of pain is a research goal rather than a reality today. The gap may be narrowed by combining different techniques. Electrophysiological methods with stimulation and recording directly from the afferent pathway should contribute to a more specific and differentiated picture of the mode of action of analgesics, as a basis for development of new therapies. Such electrophysiological methods can be combined with behavioural studies, both in humans and in animal pain models.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
